{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QTQMHB1wnNAw4dWQN8gNcs","type":"tool_result","content":"## Files in `dist/handoff/`\n\nThe directory listing is truncated; the page has a \"View all files\" link, so more files may exist.\n\n| Name | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| `docs/` | Documentation folder, including `docs/ASSETS.md` (the asset card). |\n| `game/` | Template game: `index.html`, `game.js`, `test.mjs`. |\n| `kits/` | 2D genre kits, each with a game file (`<id>.js`), a playable page (`<id>.html`), plus `README.md` and `test.mjs`. |\n| `modules/` | Individual engine modules, to load after the agent edition. |\n| `src/assets/` | Asset store of CC0 objects, materials, and sprites, with catalogs. |\n| `tools/` | Scripts such as `check.mjs`, `filmstrip.mjs`, `replay.mjs`, and the asset tools. |\n| `AI_GUIDE.md` | Recipes: genres, look, frame order, heights, and recorded sessions. |\n| `API-INDEX.md` | One-line entry for every public engine name, with signature, units, and defaults. |\n| `API.md` | The main API card: a complete starter game, coordinate meanings, rules, common mistakes, and the API by area. |\n| `README.md` | Package overview and instructions (summarized below). |\n| `index.html` | Browser page for the package. |\n| `my-3d2dge-agent.js` | Agent edition: the essential engine with a shorter manual in its header. |\n| `my-3d2dge.js` | Full engine, readable, in one file with no dependencies. |\n| `package.json` | Pins Playwright for the tools. |\n\n## README summary\n\nThe README covers package v0.85.1 of the my-3D2dge engine, which lets a coding agent build, run, test, and check a game without the engine's repository.\n\n**Start here:**\n1. Read `API.md` first.\n2. Begin from a kit or the template rather than an empty file.\n3. Search `API-INDEX.md` for names instead of reading it whole.\n4. Use `AI_GUIDE.md` for recipes.\n5. Skip building standard features like pause menus, settings, and loading screens, since the engine provides them.\n6. Read `docs/ASSETS.md` before drawing objects; use the asset tools to find and preview them.\n\n**Commands:** install dependencies, then run `game/test.mjs` (headless), `tools/check.mjs` (browser play and error checks), `kits/test.mjs` (kit test), and `tools/filmstrip.mjs` (frame recording).\n\n**Headless testing:** `new E.Game()` runs in Node without a screen. The clock uses fixed 1/120 s steps, so the same inputs produce the same result on any machine.\n\nThe README notes that the 3D engine is not included here and is hosted separately.\n\n## API documentation\n\n- **`API.md`**: the main card, covering coordinates, rules, and the API by area.\n- **`API-INDEX.md`**: a searchable index of every public name.\n- **`AI_GUIDE.md`**: implementation recipes and guidance.\n- **`docs/ASSETS.md`**: the asset API for objects and materials.\n- **`kits/README.md`**: a table describing each genre kit.\n\nI only have the listing and README text, so I can't confirm the contents of these files."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ceb3ee4-d05b-48df-8167-856a2d7758be","uuid":"324770ed-b569-4e64-82c7-f1177275cc82","timestamp":"2026-11-03T02:11:28.092Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":234268,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"## Files in `dist/handoff/`\n\nThe directory listing is truncated; the page has a \"View all files\" link, so more files may exist.\n\n| Name | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| `docs/` | Documentation folder, including `docs/ASSETS.md` (the asset card). |\n| `game/` | Template game: `index.html`, `game.js`, `test.mjs`. |\n| `kits/` | 2D genre kits, each with a game file (`<id>.js`), a playable page (`<id>.html`), plus `README.md` and `test.mjs`. |\n| `modules/` | Individual engine modules, to load after the agent edition. |\n| `src/assets/` | Asset store of CC0 objects, materials, and sprites, with catalogs. |\n| `tools/` | Scripts such as `check.mjs`, `filmstrip.mjs`, `replay.mjs`, and the asset tools. |\n| `AI_GUIDE.md` | Recipes: genres, look, frame order, heights, and recorded sessions. |\n| `API-INDEX.md` | One-line entry for every public engine name, with signature, units, and defaults. |\n| `API.md` | The main API card: a complete starter game, coordinate meanings, rules, common mistakes, and the API by area. |\n| `README.md` | Package overview and instructions (summarized below). |\n| `index.html` | Browser page for the package. |\n| `my-3d2dge-agent.js` | Agent edition: the essential engine with a shorter manual in its header. |\n| `my-3d2dge.js` | Full engine, readable, in one file with no dependencies. |\n| `package.json` | Pins Playwright for the tools. |\n\n## README summary\n\nThe README covers package v0.85.1 of the my-3D2dge engine, which lets a coding agent build, run, test, and check a game without the engine's repository.\n\n**Start here:**\n1. Read `API.md` first.\n2. Begin from a kit or the template rather than an empty file.\n3. Search `API-INDEX.md` for names instead of reading it whole.\n4. Use `AI_GUIDE.md` for recipes.\n5. Skip building standard features like pause menus, settings, and loading screens, since the engine provides them.\n6. Read `docs/ASSETS.md` before drawing objects; use the asset tools to find and preview them.\n\n**Commands:** install dependencies, then run `game/test.mjs` (headless), `tools/check.mjs` (browser play and error checks), `kits/test.mjs` (kit test), and `tools/filmstrip.mjs` (frame recording).\n\n**Headless testing:** `new E.Game()` runs in Node without a screen. The clock uses fixed 1/120 s steps, so the same inputs produce the same result on any machine.\n\nThe README notes that the 3D engine is not included here and is hosted separately.\n\n## API documentation\n\n- **`API.md`**: the main card, covering coordinates, rules, and the API by area.\n- **`API-INDEX.md`**: a searchable index of every public name.\n- **`AI_GUIDE.md`**: implementation recipes and guidance.\n- **`docs/ASSETS.md`**: the asset API for objects and materials.\n- **`kits/README.md`**: a table describing each genre kit.\n\nI only have the listing and README text, so I can't confirm the contents of these files.","durationMs":7976,"url":"https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/tree/main/dist/handoff"},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01QTQMHB1wnNAw4dWQN8gNcs","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018G88fFRFzdhJiArguH6PGL","type":"tool_result","content":"**Files in `lib/hub/`**\n\nThe directory listing shows:\n- `examples/` (folder)\n- `README.md`\n- `bridge.js`\n- `harness.html`\n- `retrofit.md`\n- `round.js`\n- `session.js`\n\nThe page also has a \"View all files\" link, so there may be more files than these.\n\n**Integration summary**\n\nThe README defines **AI Hub Session Protocol v1**. A game joins a session by following it. The page suggests adding a line like \"This game must support AI Hub sessions\" to the game's prompt.\n\n- **Modes:** A game declares one mode: `parallel` (no data exchanged), `ghost` (players share positions and actions, which don't affect other copies), or `shared-world` (the host's copy runs one world for all players). The older tags `race`, `co-op`, and `versus` map to ghost and shared-world.\n\n- **Required files:** Paste `session.js` unmodified into the game as the first script in `<head>`, right after `<meta charset>`. It seeds `Math.random` in parallel and ghost modes, isolates local and session storage, and routes fullscreen to the hub.\n\n- **Manifest (`<head>` tags):** The page doesn't describe a separate manifest file. Instead, the game sets these meta tags:\n  - Required: `hub:session` (set to `1`), `hub:session-players` (`MIN-MAX`), `hub:session-mode`, `hub:session-goal`, `hub:session-howto`\n  - Optional: `hub:session-minutes`, `hub:webgpu` (set to `required` if the game needs WebGPU)\n\n- **Lifecycle:** The game calls `AIHub.connect({ mode, seats })`, then `AIHub.ready()` once it can start. The hub sends `start`, and play begins three seconds later. The round ends with `end`.\n\n- **API:** `AIHub.active`, `connect()`, `ready()`, `time()`, `on(event, fn)`, `progress()`, `result()`, `finish()` (shared-world host only), `send()`, `rng(label)`, `fail()`. Events are `start`, `message`, `leave`, `time-up`, and `end`.\n\n- **Testing:** Serve `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, and `round.js` next to the game, then open `harness.html?game=GAME.html&players=2&auto=1`. The game passes when `window.__hubCheck.pass` is `true`.\n\n**Not covered on this page**\n\n- **Exit interview:** Not mentioned.\n- **Run record:** Not mentioned.\n- **`retrofit.md`:** Listed, but its contents aren't shown here.\n\nFor those topics, check `retrofit.md`, `examples/`, or the files behind \"View all files.\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ceb3ee4-d05b-48df-8167-856a2d7758be","uuid":"a4c8a2da-e56f-4d94-9629-706011b6300e","timestamp":"2026-11-03T02:11:28.617Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":287989,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"**Files in `lib/hub/`**\n\nThe directory listing shows:\n- `examples/` (folder)\n- `README.md`\n- `bridge.js`\n- `harness.html`\n- `retrofit.md`\n- `round.js`\n- `session.js`\n\nThe page also has a \"View all files\" link, so there may be more files than these.\n\n**Integration summary**\n\nThe README defines **AI Hub Session Protocol v1**. A game joins a session by following it. The page suggests adding a line like \"This game must support AI Hub sessions\" to the game's prompt.\n\n- **Modes:** A game declares one mode: `parallel` (no data exchanged), `ghost` (players share positions and actions, which don't affect other copies), or `shared-world` (the host's copy runs one world for all players). The older tags `race`, `co-op`, and `versus` map to ghost and shared-world.\n\n- **Required files:** Paste `session.js` unmodified into the game as the first script in `<head>`, right after `<meta charset>`. It seeds `Math.random` in parallel and ghost modes, isolates local and session storage, and routes fullscreen to the hub.\n\n- **Manifest (`<head>` tags):** The page doesn't describe a separate manifest file. Instead, the game sets these meta tags:\n  - Required: `hub:session` (set to `1`), `hub:session-players` (`MIN-MAX`), `hub:session-mode`, `hub:session-goal`, `hub:session-howto`\n  - Optional: `hub:session-minutes`, `hub:webgpu` (set to `required` if the game needs WebGPU)\n\n- **Lifecycle:** The game calls `AIHub.connect({ mode, seats })`, then `AIHub.ready()` once it can start. The hub sends `start`, and play begins three seconds later. The round ends with `end`.\n\n- **API:** `AIHub.active`, `connect()`, `ready()`, `time()`, `on(event, fn)`, `progress()`, `result()`, `finish()` (shared-world host only), `send()`, `rng(label)`, `fail()`. Events are `start`, `message`, `leave`, `time-up`, and `end`.\n\n- **Testing:** Serve `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, and `round.js` next to the game, then open `harness.html?game=GAME.html&players=2&auto=1`. The game passes when `window.__hubCheck.pass` is `true`.\n\n**Not covered on this page**\n\n- **Exit interview:** Not mentioned.\n- **Run record:** Not mentioned.\n- **`retrofit.md`:** Listed, but its contents aren't shown here.\n\nFor those topics, check `retrofit.md`, `examples/`, or the files behind \"View all files.\"","durationMs":8501,"url":"https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub"},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_018G88fFRFzdhJiArguH6PGL","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
