17:- `input.touchButtons(actions, o = {})` †: On-screen buttons for phones and tablets (shown on touch screens; the player's settings can show them always or hide them, put them on the left, and size them): input.touchButtons(['jump', 'attack'], { labels: { j\n318:- `input.touchSet(a, label = null, show = true)` †: one touch button as the moment changes: its label (TALK beside someone, NEXT in a dialog; null: its own) and whether it shows (false: nothing for it to do here). Cheap to call every step: input.touchSet('\n326:- `input.glyphs = 'auto'`: the gamepad's button symbols for label(): 'auto' (from the controller's name) | 'xbox' | 'playstation' | 'nintendo' | 'generic' (positions)\n332:- `input.names = null` †: the actions' names on the Controls screen ({ attack: 'Sword' }; false hides one from rebinding: the game's menu.controls); onBindings(b): called with the player's new bindings (the game saves and applies them)\n341:- `input.rumbleScale = .6` †: vibration strength 0..1 (0 = off; game.settings.rumble sets it)\n350:- `input.touchEnabled = true` †: false turns the touch stick off\n360:- `E.font.title(g, s, x, y, o = {})`: Big logo text for title screens: scaled glyphs with a vertical color gradient, an outline and an extruded 3D edge. title(g, 'CASTLE OF NIGHT', x, y, { scale: 3, colors: ['#fff6c8', '#ffd36a', '#e07a2a'], outline: '#1a0\n425:- `r.overlay(fn)`: draw fn(g) on top of everything, in screen pixels (HUD, dialog, menus)\n453:- `new E.Game(o = {}) → game`: new E.Game({ canvas, view, views, res, expand, input, bg, step: 1 / 120, loop: true, headless: false, menu, fullscreen: 'tap', corner: true, backGesture: true, autoPause: true, id, pace, camera }). The standard features (sect\n457:- `new E.Game({ headless })`: no screen, renderer, sound or DOM input (tests, tools, a simulation in Node, where it is the default): scenes update and draw is skipped; drive it with advance() and input.press / release / tap / hold\n469:- `game.advance(seconds = this.o.step, o = {})`: run the game for `seconds` of real time in exact fixed steps, at once, without requestAnimationFrame: tests, tools and headless runs (advance(1) is 120 updates). o.draw: then draw one frame (not in a headles\n478:- `game.flash(color = '#ffffff', seconds = .12, strength = 1)`: flash the whole screen with a color for `seconds` (dithered fade out): hits, explosions, lightning. Shorter when reduceMotion, dimmer by the player's settings.flashes\n484:- `game.menu(name)`: open the menu (the corner's menu button and the touch START do it): a pausable scene (or a game started without scenes) pauses on its pause screen; any other scene, a title, waits under the settings. menu('settings') or menu('controls'\n485:- `game.mouseGround()`: mouse position on the ground (world units), or null\n492:- `game.resetCamera()` †: undo setZoom and rotateView: the scene's own zoom again (camera.start, or camera.tall on a screen held upright; 1 without), no turn. The player's zoom stays (settings.zoom)\n495:- `game.saves()` †: game.saves: the save slots (section 10k), made when first read\n496:- `game.script(fn, o)` †: run a coroutine on game time, in the update step: game.script(function* (game) { yield .5; yield E.until(() => door.open); yield game.tween(cam, { y: 0 }, 1); yield E.all([a, b]); ... }, { keep }). Each yield waits: a number (seco\n499:- `game.shake(a)`: shake the screen by a (pixels, decaying; at most 10 in all); none when reduceMotion, scaled by the player's settings.shake\n502:- `game.start(hooks)`: Start the loop. Either one scene: game.start({ update(dt), draw(r) }) or several: game.start({ scenes: { title: {...}, play: {...} }, scene: 'title' }) A scene is { enter(data), exit(), update(dt), draw(r), back(), pausable, view, vi\n506:- `game.start({ boot })`: { title, version, steps: [[label, fn]], messages, min, checks, accent } runs the boot first (section 10c): the steps one a frame behind the boot screen (all at once when headless or loop: false); boot: false hides a splash\n511:- `game.zoomBy(k)` †: the player zooms the camera by a factor (1.1: 10% closer, .9: farther), as the wheel, - and = and a pinch do (a zoom button of the game's own can): within the scene's camera.zoom range, kept as their setting (settings.zoom, on top of \n521:- `game.drawEvery = 1`: 1, or 2 while a fast display (a 120 Hz phone) refreshes quicker than the game can draw (a frame's cost, or refreshes missed: its GPU behind): every other refresh is drawn, evenly, instead of random ones missed (the updates still run\n527:- `game.headless`: true for a game with no display (o.headless, or no DOM: Node)\n532:- `game.o`: the options the game was made with, the defaults filled in (view, res, expand, minW, minH, maxW, maxH, bg, step, input, loop, headless)\n537:- `game.r`: the renderer handed to draw(r) (null when headless)\n544:- `game.settings`: the player's choices (game.settings.volume, game.settings.set('volume', .5), your own from menu.settings), saved and applied (section 10b)\n558:- `game.zoom = 1` †: the camera's zoom now (1 = as the view is): the game's (setZoom, a scene's camera.start) times the player's (settings.zoom: the wheel, a pinch), within the scene's camera.zoom range\n564:- `settings.default(key)`: a setting's default value\n565:- `settings.define(sp)`: add a setting: { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', value, min, max, step, options: [[value, label]] or [value], help, group: 'Game', apply(game, value) }. Its saved value is loaded (when it is a valid one) and appli\n566:- `settings.keys(group)`: the keys of a group's settings, in order ('Display', 'Sound', 'Comfort', 'Controller', 'Touch', 'Game'), or every key\n567:- `settings.reset(group)`: put a group's settings (or all of them) back to their defaults; a game's saves are not touched\n568:- `settings.set(key, v)`: change a setting: checked (a slider kept in range, a choice among its options), saved, applied, onChange told. Returns the value kept (the old one when v is not a valid value)\n569:- `settings.spec(key)`: the spec a setting was defined with (its label, type, range, options), or undefined\n570:- `settings.saved`: false when the last save failed (storage blocked or full: the choices last for this visit)\n575:- `fullscreen.supported`: true where this page can go full screen (not an iPhone, which has Add to Home Screen instead; not a frame without permission; not headless)\n576:- `fullscreen.toggle()`: full screen on or off, as the player asked (the corner's button, the menu): their choice is kept in settings.fullscreen, so a game starting on a phone goes full screen by itself only while they haven't turned it off\n617:- `new E.Saves(game, o) → saves` †: game.saves (made when first read): o is menu.saves ({ slots, version, migrate, write, read })\n618:- `saves.any` †: is there any save to load (a title's Continue)?\n619:- `saves.autosave(o)` †: save to the autosave (what write() gives)\n620:- `saves.copy(from, to)` †: copy a slot's save onto another (over what is there); false when the first is empty\n621:- `saves.erase(slot)` †: erase a slot\n622:- `saves.get(slot)` †: a slot's save as it is stored, checked: null when empty; { slot, damaged: true } when it can't be read; { newer: true } from a newer version of the game; else { slot, data, place, level, time, at (the date saved), version }\n623:- `saves.latest()` †: the most recent save that loads, or null (a title's Continue loads it)\n624:- `saves.list()` †: every slot, the autosave first: [{ slot, empty, place, level, time, at, damaged, newer }] (a menu's rows)\n625:- `saves.load(slot)` †: load a slot: its data brought up to this version (migrate), played set from it, read(save) called. Returns the save ({ data, place, level, time, slot }), or null when the slot is empty, damaged or from a newer version\n626:- `saves.save(slot, o)` †: save to a slot (0.., or 'auto'): o ({ data, place, level }) or what write() gives. Returns true when it is kept (in storage, or for the visit when storage is blocked: blocked tells), false when there was nothing to save\n627:- `saves.show(mode = 'load', done)` †: open the standard save screen over the game (E.Shell's): 'save' (to a slot) or 'load'; done(save) after a load or a save. False without a menu (a headless game, menu: false)\n628:- `saves.blocked = false` †: storage refused a save (they last for the visit)\n629:- `saves.canSave = true` †: the pause menu offers Save (a JRPG turns it off away from save points)\n630:- `saves.game` †: its game\n631:- `saves.migrate` †: an older version's data brought up to this one (or null: kept as it is)\n632:- `saves.played = 0` †: seconds played in the game's scenes (paused time and titles left out), saved with each save and set by a load\n633:- `saves.read` †: what a load does with { data, place, level, time, slot }\n634:- `saves.slots` †: how many slots besides the autosave (3)\n635:- `saves.version` †: the game's version of its data (1), saved with each save\n636:- `saves.write` †: what a save holds ({ data, place, level })\n669:- `rig.drawPortrait(g, x, y, size = 40, o = {})` †: a close-up bust for dialog boxes and menus, drawn live from the rig (blinks, hair and hats included): rig.drawPortrait(g, x, y, 40, { zoom: 3, turn: .6, bg: '#1a2050', frame: true }) // inside r.overlay(g\n819:- `new E.FlowField({ jump })`: (world units) links tops across a gap that a jump clears, straight along a row or column, by map.landing's rules (up to jumpRise higher, 11, and jumpDrop lower, 18): an agent with E.Mover's leap chases across roofs. With jump\n821:- `flow.next(x, y)` †: the next cell to head for from (x, y): { x, y, z (its center and top), kind: 'walk' | 'climb' | 'drop' | 'jump', edge (how far (x, y) is from the side of its cell it leaves by) }, or null where the field doesn't reach (or at the targ\n941:- `E.ACTIONS: climbUp, climbJump, vault, hopDown, roll, getUp, takedown` †: the actions E.Action plays. Add your own: E.ACTIONS.name = { beats, setup, at }; setup(A) and at(A, beat, u) get the action: its options A.o, A.start (where the body began), A.body\n961:## 17c. Mover\n963:- `new E.Mover(o = {}) → mover`: new E.Mover({ x, y, z, r: 5, ... }): any of its fields, below, as options. An E.Body: it has body.jump, push and the body's fields too\n964:- `mover.dodge(dir, dist = 34)` †: a dodge roll toward dir (an angle or [dx, dy]; default its facing) when it stands free. Returns the action, or null\n965:- `mover.play(name, o = {})` †: start an action now (E.ACTIONS name, its options): it moves the body until it ends\n966:- `mover.respawn()` †: back to the last safe spot (after water, a pit, a fall it shouldn't survive)\n967:- `mover.rigState(extra)` †: the rig state: rig.update(dt, hero.rigState({ attack })): its motion, crouch, sprint and landing, or the playing action's pose; extra is merged over it\n968:- `mover.update(dt, map, ctl = {}, view)` †: one step. ctl: game.input (needs the actions move, jump, and sprint / crouch if it has them; screen directions turn into ground ones through view, the game's by default) or an intent { move: [dx, dy], sprint, cr\n969:- `mover.accel = 700`, `mover.airAccel = 260` †: how fast it gets there\n970:- `mover.action = null` †: the E.Action playing, or null\n971:- `mover.buffer = .12` †: seconds a jump press is kept\n972:- `mover.climb = true` †: climbs ledges (true)\n973:- `mover.climbAny = false` †: climbs any wall face (see the section's header)\n974:- `mover.climbMax = 82` †: the highest ledge it climbs\n975:- `mover.climbSpeed = 34` †: its climbing speed\n976:- `mover.coyote = .1` †: seconds a jump still works after leaving an edge\n977:- `mover.crouch = false` †: sneaking (a toggle)\n978:- `mover.exhausted = false` †: out of stamina until a third is back\n979:- `mover.facing = 0` †: the angle it faces\n980:- `mover.fell = 0`, `mover.hurt = false`, `mover.inHazard = false` †: what happened this step\n981:- `mover.gapAssist = true` †: a jump at a gap aims for the far side\n982:- `mover.glide = false` †: opens a glide in the air (see the header)\n983:- `mover.glideMin = 24`, `mover.glideSink = 26`, `mover.glideSpeed = 72` †: how high over the ground it opens, how fast it sinks and flies\n984:- `mover.gliding = false` †: gliding now\n985:- `mover.hopMax = 48` †: drops up to this deep are hopped down\n986:- `mover.hurtAt = 72`, `mover.rollAt = 26` †: fall heights that roll and that hurt\n987:- `mover.jumpSpeed = 220` †: a jump's upward speed\n988:- `mover.lastSafe = null` †: the last spot it stood safely, for respawn()\n989:- `mover.lift = 0` †: an updraft's rising speed (a number, or a function of the mover)\n990:- `mover.run = 85`, `mover.sneak = 32`, `mover.sprintSpeed = 125`, `mover.walk = 50` †: top speeds (world units a second)\n991:- `mover.sprinting = false` †: sprinting now\n992:- `mover.stamina` †: what is left (full to start)\n993:- `mover.staminaMax = 0` †: its stamina (0: none)\n994:- `mover.staminaRegen = 35` †: refilled a second standing","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium__20261102-191111__x3ec78e/work","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01SXmTWjYM1govQyjLFAwhLt","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgfBdxSPcz9o4RD4mPBoS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UmYiGQ9AVgWmRws1vMwC4T","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/ref-engine && cat game/test.mjs | head -80; echo ----; cat game/index.html; echo ----; grep -n \"</script\" my-3d2dge.js | head; grep -c \"\" my-3d2dge.js","description":"Read template test, index page, and check script-tag safety"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1832,"cache_read_input_tokens":74069,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1832,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ceb3ee4-d05b-48df-8167-856a2d7758be","uuid":"700bf5e0-e5ed-45a1-a3ff-85ee2dc2a61a","timestamp":"2026-11-03T02:12:34.168Z","request_id":"req_011CgfBdx5KtHmxYo4pFkQAP","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01UmYiGQ9AVgWmRws1vMwC4T":{"command":"cd /tmp/ref-engine && cat game/test.mjs | head -80; echo ----; cat game/index.html; echo ----; grep -n \"</script\" my-3d2dge.js | head; grep -c \"\" my-3d2dge.js","description":"Read template test, index page, and check script-tag safety"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UmYiGQ9AVgWmRws1vMwC4T","type":"tool_result","content":"// A headless test of the template game: the engine and game.js run in Node with no screen (new E.Game is headless where\n// there is no DOM), driven by fixed steps (game.advance) and scripted input (input.tap, input.hold), and read through\n// game.debug.snapshot(). Run it: node game/test.mjs (exit code 1 on a failure). Write one like it for your game.\nimport vm from 'node:vm';\nimport { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\n\nconst ctx = { console };\nvm.createContext(ctx);\nfor (const f of ['../my-3d2dge.js', './game.js']) vm.runInContext(readFileSync(new URL(f, import.meta.url), 'utf8'), ctx, { filename: f });\nconst E = ctx.My3D2dge, game = E.current, I = game.input, snap = () => game.debug.snapshot();\nlet failed = 0;\nconst check = (what, ok, detail = '') => { console.log((ok ? 'ok   ' : 'FAIL ') + what + (ok ? '' : ': ' + detail)); if (!ok) failed++; };\n\ngame.advance(.5);\ncheck('the title waits for start', snap().scene === 'title', JSON.stringify(snap()));\nI.tap('start'); game.advance(.5);\ncheck('start begins play', snap().scene === 'play', JSON.stringify(snap()));\n\n// climb: stand facing the roof's west wall (cells 7-9 of rows 4-6: x 112-160, y 64-112), press jump to take hold, then\n// climb with up (up the screen is up the wall) until it pulls up onto the top\ngame.debug.teleport(100, 88, 0, 0);\nI.tap('jump'); game.advance(.1);\ncheck('jump next to a wall takes hold of it', snap().climbing, JSON.stringify(snap()));\nI.hold('up'); game.advance(.6); I.hold('up', false); game.advance(1);\ncheck('climbing up pulls up onto the roof', !snap().climbing && snap().hero[2] === 32, JSON.stringify(snap()));\n\n// take the gem (on the roof's middle cell), then hop down into the street with it\ngame.debug.teleport(136, 88, 32, 0); game.advance(.1);\ncheck('walking onto the gem takes it', snap().got, JSON.stringify(snap()));\ngame.debug.teleport(156, 120, 32, Math.PI / 2); I.hold('down'); game.advance(1.5); I.hold('down', false); game.advance(.5);\ncheck('back in the street with the gem wins', snap().scene === 'end' && snap().won, JSON.stringify(snap()));\n\n// get seen: stand in front of the guard, in the open, until its alert fills\nI.tap('start'); game.advance(.5);\nconst [gx, gy, gf] = snap().guard;\ngame.debug.teleport(gx + Math.cos(gf) * 40, gy + Math.sin(gf) * 40, 0, gf + Math.PI);\ngame.advance(2.5);\ncheck('the guard catches a hero it sees', snap().scene === 'end' && !snap().won, JSON.stringify(snap()));\ncheck('no errors', !game.errors.length, game.errors.map(e => e.message).join(' | '));\n\nconsole.log(failed ? `${failed} check(s) failed` : 'all checks passed');\nprocess.exit(failed ? 1 : 0);\n----\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\">\n<title>Rooftop · my-3D2dge template</title>\n<style>html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; background: #000; overflow: hidden } #screen { width: 100%; height: 100%; display: block; image-rendering: pixelated; touch-action: none }</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div id=\"e3-boot\" role=\"status\" style=\"position:fixed;inset:0;z-index:40;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:flex-end;gap:6px;padding:20px;background:#05040a;color:#a9a1c8;font:12px/1.5 ui-monospace,Menlo,Consolas,monospace\"><style>@keyframes e3-run{from{transform:translateX(-100%)}to{transform:translateX(340%)}}@keyframes e3-late{to{opacity:1}}</style><b style=\"color:#f4f0ff;font-size:16px;letter-spacing:.08em\">ROOFTOP</b><span>Starting · my-3D2dge v0.85.1</span><span style=\"display:block;height:4px;max-width:440px;overflow:hidden;background:#ffffff14\"><span style=\"display:block;width:30%;height:100%;background:#d9b77c;animation:e3-run 1.2s ease-in-out infinite\"></span></span><span style=\"opacity:0;animation:e3-late .3s 12s forwards\">Still starting. If this stays, the game's script did not run: reload, or open the browser's console.</span></div>\n<canvas id=\"screen\"></canvas>\n<script src=\"../my-3d2dge.js\"></script>\n<script src=\"game.js\"></script>\n</body>\n</html>\n----\n14706\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium__20261102-191111__x3ec78e/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ceb3ee4-d05b-48df-8167-856a2d7758be","uuid":"6ef17b46-86d5-4e75-9826-eac06c8e6c88","timestamp":"2026-11-03T02:12:34.208Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"// A headless test of the template game: the engine and game.js run in Node with no screen (new E.Game is headless where\n// there is no DOM), driven by fixed steps (game.advance) and scripted input (input.tap, input.hold), and read through\n// game.debug.snapshot(). Run it: node game/test.mjs (exit code 1 on a failure). Write one like it for your game.\nimport vm from 'node:vm';\nimport { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\n\nconst ctx = { console };\nvm.createContext(ctx);\nfor (const f of ['../my-3d2dge.js', './game.js']) vm.runInContext(readFileSync(new URL(f, import.meta.url), 'utf8'), ctx, { filename: f });\nconst E = ctx.My3D2dge, game = E.current, I = game.input, snap = () => game.debug.snapshot();\nlet failed = 0;\nconst check = (what, ok, detail = '') => { console.log((ok ? 'ok   ' : 'FAIL ') + what + (ok ? '' : ': ' + detail)); if (!ok) failed++; };\n\ngame.advance(.5);\ncheck('the title waits for start', snap().scene === 'title', JSON.stringify(snap()));\nI.tap('start'); game.advance(.5);\ncheck('start begins play', snap().scene === 'play', JSON.stringify(snap()));\n\n// climb: stand facing the roof's west wall (cells 7-9 of rows 4-6: x 112-160, y 64-112), press jump to take hold, then\n// climb with up (up the screen is up the wall) until it pulls up onto the top\ngame.debug.teleport(100, 88, 0, 0);\nI.tap('jump'); game.advance(.1);\ncheck('jump next to a wall takes hold of it', snap().climbing, JSON.stringify(snap()));\nI.hold('up'); game.advance(.6); I.hold('up', false); game.advance(1);\ncheck('climbing up pulls up onto the roof', !snap().climbing && snap().hero[2] === 32, JSON.stringify(snap()));\n\n// take the gem (on the roof's middle cell), then hop down into the street with it\ngame.debug.teleport(136, 88, 32, 0); game.advance(.1);\ncheck('walking onto the gem takes it', snap().got, JSON.stringify(snap()));\ngame.debug.teleport(156, 120, 32, Math.PI / 2); I.hold('down'); game.advance(1.5); I.hold('down', false); game.advance(.5);\ncheck('back in the street with the gem wins', snap().scene === 'end' && snap().won, JSON.stringify(snap()));\n\n// get seen: stand in front of the guard, in the open, until its alert fills\nI.tap('start'); game.advance(.5);\nconst [gx, gy, gf] = snap().guard;\ngame.debug.teleport(gx + Math.cos(gf) * 40, gy + Math.sin(gf) * 40, 0, gf + Math.PI);\ngame.advance(2.5);\ncheck('the guard catches a hero it sees', snap().scene === 'end' && !snap().won, JSON.stringify(snap()));\ncheck('no errors', !game.errors.length, game.errors.map(e => e.message).join(' | '));\n\nconsole.log(failed ? `${failed} check(s) failed` : 'all checks passed');\nprocess.exit(failed ? 1 : 0);\n----\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\">\n<title>Rooftop · my-3D2dge template</title>\n<style>html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; background: #000; overflow: hidden } #screen { width: 100%; height: 100%; display: block; image-rendering: pixelated; touch-action: none }</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div id=\"e3-boot\" role=\"status\" style=\"position:fixed;inset:0;z-index:40;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:flex-end;gap:6px;padding:20px;background:#05040a;color:#a9a1c8;font:12px/1.5 ui-monospace,Menlo,Consolas,monospace\"><style>@keyframes e3-run{from{transform:translateX(-100%)}to{transform:translateX(340%)}}@keyframes e3-late{to{opacity:1}}</style><b style=\"color:#f4f0ff;font-size:16px;letter-spacing:.08em\">ROOFTOP</b><span>Starting · my-3D2dge v0.85.1</span><span style=\"display:block;height:4px;max-width:440px;overflow:hidden;background:#ffffff14\"><span style=\"display:block;width:30%;height:100%;background:#d9b77c;animation:e3-run 1.2s ease-in-out infinite\"></span></span><span style=\"opacity:0;animation:e3-late .3s 12s forwards\">Still starting. If this stays, the game's script did not run: reload, or open the browser's console.</span></div>\n<canvas id=\"screen\"></canvas>\n<script src=\"../my-3d2dge.js\"></script>\n<script src=\"game.js\"></script>\n</body>\n</html>\n----\n14706","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium__20261102-191111__x3ec78e/work","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01UmYiGQ9AVgWmRws1vMwC4T","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
