{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JYxTSWAMBym8eLAp4cenpu","type":"tool_result","content":"69:- 638 Humanoid rig; E.Attack: slash, E.Combo: combo, E.Humanoid: rig\n80:- 1000 17d. Perception; E.Suspicion: suspicion\n81:- 1017 Bullets; E.Bullets: shots\n296:- `input.move()`: movement intent in screen directions: x right, y down, length <= 1\n483:- `game.hitFx(x, y, z, o = {})`: everything a good hit needs in one call: hit-stop, shake, an impact star, sparks along the hit direction, a sound, a damage number and a rumble on a gamepad. hitFx(x, y, z, { power: 1, angle, damage, color, sound: 'hit', rumble: true })\n544:- `game.settings`: the player's choices (game.settings.volume, game.settings.set('volume', .5), your own from menu.settings), saved and applied (section 10b)\n570:- `settings.saved`: false when the last save failed (storage blocked or full: the choices last for this visit)\n640:- `new E.Attack(spec = {}, over) → slash`: new E.Attack(spec) or new E.Attack('slash', { reach: 9 }): a name from E.MOVES plus overrides\n653:- `new E.Combo(specs, o = {}) → combo`: new E.Combo(items, { window: .3 }): items are move names, specs or Attacks\n703:- `E.MOVES: slash, backslash, overhead, rising, thrust, spin, plunge, twohand, jab, cross, hook, uppercut, haymaker, elbow, ... (24)`: a library of named attacks with timing and body motion (anticipation, lunge, step, twist, hop). new E.Attack('overhead'), new E.Attack('thrust', { reach: 10 }), new E.Combo(['jab', 'cross', '\n708:- `E.knockback(from, target, speed = 160, up = 0)`: push a target away from a point (attacker): uses target.push (E.Body) or its vx / vy. up = upward speed (knock into the air)\n880:- `new E.Platformer(o = {}) → hero`: a side-scroller character body with modern, forgiving controls (coyote time, jump buffering, variable jump height, optional double jump, wall jump, dash, ladders, knockback). const hero = new E.Platformer({ x, z, w: 8, h: 22 }); update: hero.update(dt, level, game.input) (or an intent obj\n885:- `hero.update(dt, level, ctl = {}, solids)`: move it one step: ctl is game.input or an intent { x: -1..1, jump, jumpPressed, up, down, dash } (enemies, bots); solids: moving platforms [{ x, z, w, h, vx, vz }] to stand on\n911:- `hero.stun = 0`: seconds of knockback left (no control)\n923:- `body.push(ix, iy, iz = 0)`: add an impulse (knockback, explosion): push(vx, vy, vz)\n968:- `mover.update(dt, map, ctl = {}, view)` †: one step. ctl: game.input (needs the actions move, jump, and sprint / crouch if it has them; screen directions turn into ground ones through view, the game's by default) or an intent { move: [dx, dy], sprint, crouch, jumpPressed }\n1002:- `new E.Suspicion(o = {}) → suspicion`: new E.Suspicion({ rise, decay, notice, search, alert, forget }): a guard's mind (its fields, below, are its options). Its level rises while it sees the target (faster the more exposed and nearer), decays while it doesn't, and names a state: 'calm', 'notice' (turn and look), 'search' \n1005:- `suspicion.update(dt, seen, target)` †: one step: seen is E.sees' result (or true / false), target the body seen. Returns the state\n1015:- `E.sees(obs, tgt, o = {})`: can observer see target? { seen, d (ground distance), angle (observer -> target), exposure: 0..1 }. The target must be within range and inside the cone fov wide (radians) about the observer's facing; exposure is the share of three points on it (its feet, its chest, its head) that the observer's\n1019:- `new E.Bullets(game, o = {}) → shots`: new E.Bullets(game, { plane: 'ground' | 'side', max: 800, sparks: true }); game: its game\n1020:- `shots.burst(base, vels)`: fire several at once from a pattern list of [vx, v2] (v2 = vy on the ground plane, vz in side view)\n1021:- `shots.clear(team)`: remove every bullet, or only one team's\n1022:- `shots.draw(r)`: queue them for drawing (glowing cores, or their sprites)\n1023:- `shots.fire(b)`: fire one bullet. Fields: x, y, z, vx, vy, vz, r, dmg, life, team, color, core, sprite, pierce, grav, data\n1024:- `shots.hit(targets, fn, team)`: test bullets of `team` against targets (objects with x, y, z and r, or w/h in side view). fn(bullet, target). Returns hits\n1025:- `shots.update(dt, map)`: move them one step; with a map they stop at walls (a TileMap, or a PlatformMap in side views)\n1026:- `shots.list = []`: the live bullets\n1027:- `shots.max`: at most this many at once\n1028:- `shots.plane`: 'ground' (they fly over x and y) or 'side' (x and z)\n1029:- `shots.sparks`: a puff of sparks where one hits a wall\n1054:- `game.audio.define(name, voice)`: add or replace a named sound: audio.define('zap', { wave: 'saw', freq: 1200, to: 200, dur: .2 })\n1063:- `game.audio.sfx(what, o = {})`: Play a sound effect: a preset name ('jump', 'coin', 'hit', 'explode', ...), a voice object, or a list of voices. opts: { vol: 0..1, pitch: multiplier, vary: random pitch spread (default 0.03), step: a step of the music playing (it sounds on that step of the music clock, scheduled with the m\n1075:- `game.audio.presets`: the named sound effects, sfx(name) plays one and define(name, voice) adds one\n1106:- `new E.Dialog(game, o = {}) → talk`: new E.Dialog(game, { speed, lines, place, color, nameColor, voice, bg, border, vars }): a dialog box that types its text; say() opens it, update(dt) and draw(r) run it\n1107:- `talk.choiceAt(i)` †: where choice i is on the screen while the choices show: [x, y] (its middle, for a test's tap), else null\n1111:- `talk.say(text, o = {})`: open with one string or a list of strings (each starts a new page). opts: { name, onDone, choices, onChoice, portrait: rig (a live close-up of that Humanoid beside the text) or a function (g, x, y, size), portraitSize: 40, portraitOpts: { zoom, turn, bg }, auto: seconds a page shows before it tur\n1117:- `talk.choices`: the answers offered on the last page, or null\n1134:- `talk.voice = 'text'`: the sound effect each letter blips ('text'; null for silence)\n1306:- `car.update(dt, map, c = {})`: one step: steering, engine, grip, drift, the surface, then E.Body's walls and hop. c: an input or an intent\n1324:- `race.drive(R, dt)`: a racer's way round: the intent race.update gives an AI racer's car (look ahead along the line, bends, overtakes, unsticking, the rubber band)\n1342:- `fightai.intent(f, foe, dt)` †: what it does this step: an intent for fighter f.update(dt, intent) ({ x, y: -1..1 on screen, press, do })\n1370:- `fighter.update(dt, ctl = this.input)` †: move one step (once a step, 120 times a second): ctl is its E.Input (this.input by default) or a CPU's intent\n1384:- `fighter.input` †: its E.Input, or null (a CPU passes its intent to update)\n1397:- `fighter.shots` †: its projectiles (E.Bullets, the side plane)\n1466:- `gridmover.update(dt, grid, want, o = {})`: a step of dt: want ([dx, dy] or null) is kept until it can be taken. o: { blocked(cx, cy): true where it can't go, push(cx, cy, dx, dy): true when what is in the way moved (a crate), keep: true goes on in the same direction (a maze) }. Returns true when it reached a cell this st\n1543:- `new E.Rhythm(game, o = {}) → rhythm` †: new E.Rhythm(game, { song, chart, lanes, windows, life, lead, voice, on }): see the manual\n1570:- `rhythm.voice` †: the calls' sound\n1671:- `story.skip = false`: pages type at once and turn at once (choices still wait)\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium__20261102-191111__x3ec78e/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ceb3ee4-d05b-48df-8167-856a2d7758be","uuid":"9f5c8da2-a81a-4b7f-b4a9-c570dc24a1b9","timestamp":"2026-11-03T02:12:37.694Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"69:- 638 Humanoid rig; E.Attack: slash, E.Combo: combo, E.Humanoid: rig\n80:- 1000 17d. Perception; E.Suspicion: suspicion\n81:- 1017 Bullets; E.Bullets: shots\n296:- `input.move()`: movement intent in screen directions: x right, y down, length <= 1\n483:- `game.hitFx(x, y, z, o = {})`: everything a good hit needs in one call: hit-stop, shake, an impact star, sparks along the hit direction, a sound, a damage number and a rumble on a gamepad. hitFx(x, y, z, { power: 1, angle, damage, color, sound: 'hit', rumble: true })\n544:- `game.settings`: the player's choices (game.settings.volume, game.settings.set('volume', .5), your own from menu.settings), saved and applied (section 10b)\n570:- `settings.saved`: false when the last save failed (storage blocked or full: the choices last for this visit)\n640:- `new E.Attack(spec = {}, over) → slash`: new E.Attack(spec) or new E.Attack('slash', { reach: 9 }): a name from E.MOVES plus overrides\n653:- `new E.Combo(specs, o = {}) → combo`: new E.Combo(items, { window: .3 }): items are move names, specs or Attacks\n703:- `E.MOVES: slash, backslash, overhead, rising, thrust, spin, plunge, twohand, jab, cross, hook, uppercut, haymaker, elbow, ... (24)`: a library of named attacks with timing and body motion (anticipation, lunge, step, twist, hop). new E.Attack('overhead'), new E.Attack('thrust', { reach: 10 }), new E.Combo(['jab', 'cross', '\n708:- `E.knockback(from, target, speed = 160, up = 0)`: push a target away from a point (attacker): uses target.push (E.Body) or its vx / vy. up = upward speed (knock into the air)\n880:- `new E.Platformer(o = {}) → hero`: a side-scroller character body with modern, forgiving controls (coyote time, jump buffering, variable jump height, optional double jump, wall jump, dash, ladders, knockback). const hero = new E.Platformer({ x, z, w: 8, h: 22 }); update: hero.update(dt, level, game.input) (or an intent obj\n885:- `hero.update(dt, level, ctl = {}, solids)`: move it one step: ctl is game.input or an intent { x: -1..1, jump, jumpPressed, up, down, dash } (enemies, bots); solids: moving platforms [{ x, z, w, h, vx, vz }] to stand on\n911:- `hero.stun = 0`: seconds of knockback left (no control)\n923:- `body.push(ix, iy, iz = 0)`: add an impulse (knockback, explosion): push(vx, vy, vz)\n968:- `mover.update(dt, map, ctl = {}, view)` †: one step. ctl: game.input (needs the actions move, jump, and sprint / crouch if it has them; screen directions turn into ground ones through view, the game's by default) or an intent { move: [dx, dy], sprint, crouch, jumpPressed }\n1002:- `new E.Suspicion(o = {}) → suspicion`: new E.Suspicion({ rise, decay, notice, search, alert, forget }): a guard's mind (its fields, below, are its options). Its level rises while it sees the target (faster the more exposed and nearer), decays while it doesn't, and names a state: 'calm', 'notice' (turn and look), 'search' \n1005:- `suspicion.update(dt, seen, target)` †: one step: seen is E.sees' result (or true / false), target the body seen. Returns the state\n1015:- `E.sees(obs, tgt, o = {})`: can observer see target? { seen, d (ground distance), angle (observer -> target), exposure: 0..1 }. The target must be within range and inside the cone fov wide (radians) about the observer's facing; exposure is the share of three points on it (its feet, its chest, its head) that the observer's\n1019:- `new E.Bullets(game, o = {}) → shots`: new E.Bullets(game, { plane: 'ground' | 'side', max: 800, sparks: true }); game: its game\n1020:- `shots.burst(base, vels)`: fire several at once from a pattern list of [vx, v2] (v2 = vy on the ground plane, vz in side view)\n1021:- `shots.clear(team)`: remove every bullet, or only one team's\n1022:- `shots.draw(r)`: queue them for drawing (glowing cores, or their sprites)\n1023:- `shots.fire(b)`: fire one bullet. Fields: x, y, z, vx, vy, vz, r, dmg, life, team, color, core, sprite, pierce, grav, data\n1024:- `shots.hit(targets, fn, team)`: test bullets of `team` against targets (objects with x, y, z and r, or w/h in side view). fn(bullet, target). Returns hits\n1025:- `shots.update(dt, map)`: move them one step; with a map they stop at walls (a TileMap, or a PlatformMap in side views)\n1026:- `shots.list = []`: the live bullets\n1027:- `shots.max`: at most this many at once\n1028:- `shots.plane`: 'ground' (they fly over x and y) or 'side' (x and z)\n1029:- `shots.sparks`: a puff of sparks where one hits a wall\n1054:- `game.audio.define(name, voice)`: add or replace a named sound: audio.define('zap', { wave: 'saw', freq: 1200, to: 200, dur: .2 })\n1063:- `game.audio.sfx(what, o = {})`: Play a sound effect: a preset name ('jump', 'coin', 'hit', 'explode', ...), a voice object, or a list of voices. opts: { vol: 0..1, pitch: multiplier, vary: random pitch spread (default 0.03), step: a step of the music playing (it sounds on that step of the music clock, scheduled with the m\n1075:- `game.audio.presets`: the named sound effects, sfx(name) plays one and define(name, voice) adds one\n1106:- `new E.Dialog(game, o = {}) → talk`: new E.Dialog(game, { speed, lines, place, color, nameColor, voice, bg, border, vars }): a dialog box that types its text; say() opens it, update(dt) and draw(r) run it\n1107:- `talk.choiceAt(i)` †: where choice i is on the screen while the choices show: [x, y] (its middle, for a test's tap), else null\n1111:- `talk.say(text, o = {})`: open with one string or a list of strings (each starts a new page). opts: { name, onDone, choices, onChoice, portrait: rig (a live close-up of that Humanoid beside the text) or a function (g, x, y, size), portraitSize: 40, portraitOpts: { zoom, turn, bg }, auto: seconds a page shows before it tur\n1117:- `talk.choices`: the answers offered on the last page, or null\n1134:- `talk.voice = 'text'`: the sound effect each letter blips ('text'; null for silence)\n1306:- `car.update(dt, map, c = {})`: one step: steering, engine, grip, drift, the surface, then E.Body's walls and hop. c: an input or an intent\n1324:- `race.drive(R, dt)`: a racer's way round: the intent race.update gives an AI racer's car (look ahead along the line, bends, overtakes, unsticking, the rubber band)\n1342:- `fightai.intent(f, foe, dt)` †: what it does this step: an intent for fighter f.update(dt, intent) ({ x, y: -1..1 on screen, press, do })\n1370:- `fighter.update(dt, ctl = this.input)` †: move one step (once a step, 120 times a second): ctl is its E.Input (this.input by default) or a CPU's intent\n1384:- `fighter.input` †: its E.Input, or null (a CPU passes its intent to update)\n1397:- `fighter.shots` †: its projectiles (E.Bullets, the side plane)\n1466:- `gridmover.update(dt, grid, want, o = {})`: a step of dt: want ([dx, dy] or null) is kept until it can be taken. o: { blocked(cx, cy): true where it can't go, push(cx, cy, dx, dy): true when what is in the way moved (a crate), keep: true goes on in the same direction (a maze) }. Returns true when it reached a cell this st\n1543:- `new E.Rhythm(game, o = {}) → rhythm` †: new E.Rhythm(game, { song, chart, lanes, windows, life, lead, voice, on }): see the manual\n1570:- `rhythm.voice` †: the calls' sound\n1671:- `story.skip = false`: pages type at once and turn at once (choices still wait)","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium__20261102-191111__x3ec78e/work","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01JYxTSWAMBym8eLAp4cenpu","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
