{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgfBpDxq2vCQZ5VBRNPA1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016wLr1g3a67ioUYhQaqsHGq","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/ref-engine && grep -n -E \"flow\\.dir|\\.press\\(\\)|\\.hits\\(|map\\.sight|\\bsight\\(|settings\\.define|\\.center\\(|\\.update\\(tx|E\\.inArc|r\\.textAt|r\\.shape\\(|\\.prop\\(|r\\.actor\\(\" API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-420 | head -30","description":"Grep key method signatures in API index"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1283,"cache_read_input_tokens":116631,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1283,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ceb3ee4-d05b-48df-8167-856a2d7758be","uuid":"32551030-48de-44f5-a711-1145eb8272ee","timestamp":"2026-11-03T02:15:20.141Z","request_id":"req_011CgfBpDazrtdcpMikGTdLw","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_016wLr1g3a67ioUYhQaqsHGq":{"command":"cd /tmp/ref-engine && grep -n -E \"flow\\.dir|\\.press\\(\\)|\\.hits\\(|map\\.sight|\\bsight\\(|settings\\.define|\\.center\\(|\\.update\\(tx|E\\.inArc|r\\.textAt|r\\.shape\\(|\\.prop\\(|r\\.actor\\(\" API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-420 | head -30","description":"Grep key method signatures in API index"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016wLr1g3a67ioUYhQaqsHGq","type":"tool_result","content":"20:- Collision, standing, sight (`map.sight`, `map.ray`), reach (`E.targets`, `E.inArc` with `dz`) and navigation (`E.FlowField`) all follow these rules. `E.dist` is 3D; `E.overlap` is flat.\n41:if (!map.sight(guard, hero)) throw new Error('eyes on a roof see down into the street');\n166:- `E.inArc(a, facing, b, range, halfAngle, dz)`: melee cone on the ground: is b (with optional radius r) within range of a and within halfAngle of facing? dz (optional) also limits the height difference, so a hero on a roof can't hit a guard in the street (left out, height is ignored)\n407:- `r.actor(x, y, z, drawFn, o = {})`: Queue a character. drawFn(g, ox, oy) must draw with (ox, oy) as the projected position of world point (x, y, z). The engine adds outline, rim light, hit flash, afterimages and x-ray silhouettes. opts: {outline=true, rim=true, flash=false, alpha=1, xray=false, ghost:{color, life, alpha, owner}, hides, bias, every, key, emissive (it stays bright under lighting, as r.queue's)}\n408:- `r.actor({ xray })`: true shows the actor's hidden part (a translucent tint with a 1-px outline, r.xrayColor and r.xrayOutline; a checker in E.style.trans 'dither') wherever a wall, a prop or shape at least chest high, or anything queued with hides is drawn in front of it (not one rising less than E.HEIGHTS.level, 8, above its feet: the roof it stands on, a cut-down wall); xray: { color, outline (false: none), \n409:- `r.actor({ hides })`: true: this actor counts as an x-ray occluder even when no x-ray actor asked for actors\n410:- `r.actor({ ghost })`: ghost.owner (any {x, y, z}, usually the actor itself) keeps its afterimages sorted behind the live body\n411:- `r.actor({ every, key })`: every: n, key (any object, the character's own): its finished image is drawn again for n - 1 frames before drawFn runs again, at the place it is now (a background character animating at a lower rate, as classic games' townsfolk do: a phone's frame keeps the time for the ones that matter); not while it flashes, with a ghost, x-ray or GPU lighting\n412:- `r.actor({ wrap })`: [w, h], as r.sprite's: a world that wraps round shows the actor across each edge it crosses\n426:- `r.pick(sx, sy)` †: what was drawn under a screen point (the HUD's pixels: input.clicked(), input.pointer()) in the last frame, front to back: the pick values of the actors, sprites, props and queued draws given one (r.actor(x, y, z, fn, { pick: unit })), each where its pixels went (an actor's drawn bounds; others' box, or a body's size round its point). [] for none\n427:- `r.prop(name, x, y, z, o = {})` †: set dressing from E.prop: r.prop('torch', x, y, z, { size, color, flip, light: true, halo: true, bias, hides, footprint }) feet on the world point; flames animate and glow. light: true also adds a warm light to game.lights. A prop at least chest high (E.HEIGHTS.chest, 22: a pillar, a statue, a lamp) drawn in front of an x-ray actor shows the actor's silhouette through it; a lo\n430:- `r.shape(id, x, y, z = 0, o = {})` †: Queue a shape standing at (x, y, z), feet on the point, depth sorted like an actor: r.shape(id | entry, x, y, z, o). o: { facing (radians, where its front points; default PI/2, south, as written), scale, mats: { slot: material }, flip (mirror it x to -x before facing), params (a generator's: { h: 30 }), bias, hides (x-ray silhouettes show through it: by default when it stan\n436:- `r.textAt(x, y, z, str, color = '#ffffff', o = {})`: text floating at a world point (names, prompts): r.textAt(x, y, z, 'OPEN', '#ffe08a')\n565:- `settings.define(sp)`: add a setting: { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', value, min, max, step, options: [[value, label]] or [value], help, group: 'Game', apply(game, value) }. Its saved value is loaded (when it is a valid one) and applied; it shows on the settings screen. Returns its value\n644:- `slash.hits(targets, test, fn)`: during 'active', call fn(target) once per swing for each target where test(target) is true. Returns how many were hit\n658:- `combo.hits(targets, test, fn)`: the current hit's hits(targets, test, fn): fn(target) once per swing where test(target) is true\n659:- `combo.press()`: start or continue the chain. Returns true if a hit started\n745:- `map.center(cx, cy)`: the world point at a cell's center\n760:- `map.los(x0, y0, x1, y1)`: line of sight across the ground (true if nothing solid in between). It ignores heights: sight() is the one that sees over a low wall and from a roof\n766:- `map.sight(a, b, o = {})`: can a's eyes (z + eye) see b's chest (z + chest)? E.HEIGHTS gives both unless o ({ eye, target }) or the bodies' own eye and chest say otherwise. A guard sees over a planter lower than its eyes, and down from a roof\n820:- `flow.dir(x, y, fx, fy)`: normalized ground direction to walk from (x, y) toward the target (straight at it where the field doesn't reach)\n850:- `level.center(cx, cz)`: a cell's center -> [x, z]\n1089:- `E.PROPS: torch, candle, candelabra, chandelier, brazier, window, banner, pillar, statue, crate, barrel, chest, pot, sign, fence, lamp, door, tree, pine, bush, flowers, grass, rock, crystal, bones, skull, vines, cobweb, lantern, streetlamp, awning, hydrant, trashcan, firedrum, sandbags, cactus, palm, mushroom` †: the names of the built-in props for r.prop(name, x, y, z, opts) and E.prop(name, opts)\n1090:- `E.prop(name, o = {})`: build (and cache) a prop: { frames: [sprite], glow: [sprite] | null, w, h }\n1441:- `grid.center(c, T = 16)`: a cell's centre in world units, T a cell across (square: T wide; hex: T across its flats)\n1580:- `road.hits(z, x, w)`: the scenery a body w half roads wide at (z, x) touches\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium__20261102-191111__x3ec78e/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ceb3ee4-d05b-48df-8167-856a2d7758be","uuid"